{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786999214436884001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"berkelium-active-eskimodog","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5f8c110d4938c818953d35c6ce4e53f995979f249a02ea01b3e16580acfa3f81","event_uuid":"181009ae-b84a-4ff8-9ad2-057ef34ce7b0","position":{"commit_sha":"c298d84744191093d28ab7a3950e0c2e462b01c6","position":"1786994108365090001-181009ae-b84a-4ff8-9ad2-057ef34ce7b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4789989cfca15d8b548e5a78a828aaae38a035aafd8a4d0df0bc6e0b818d963a","event_uuid":"e731df12-a2e8-45f9-8b4a-d435ee98f99d","position":{"commit_sha":"2042e45e967f96994e3d8897fff3851f0b3cbe2d","position":"1786994134264945001-e731df12-a2e8-45f9-8b4a-d435ee98f99d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a1c11a57b2bef6157c1e109a6bec3473ef8e2053b668c0315e25df76363cdc4c","event_uuid":"5bf42091-1145-4b1f-96dc-4c7dc3bbab09","position":{"commit_sha":"28368033399bae8c725a9161295ac77cfc24969f","position":"1786994147424487001-5bf42091-1145-4b1f-96dc-4c7dc3bbab09"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786994108365090001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e731df12-a2e8-45f9-8b4a-d435ee98f99d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f643-db7d-3d9c-4bd3"},{"link_uuid":"5bf42091-1145-4b1f-96dc-4c7dc3bbab09","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"368f-f03e-a045-4377"}],"description":"## Summary\nThe scheduled **Live External Integration** run on 2026-08-17 (run 32000764439, job \"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\") failed\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py::test_capability_stamp_and_fail_closed`\nwith:\n\n```\nE   subprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['git', 'commit', '-q', '--no-verify', '-m', 'commit scratch mapping (368f scenario 9)']' returned non-zero exit status 1.\n...\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n```\n\nScenario 9 writes a bridge-project mapping via `rebar.bridge_projects_set(...)` into the throwaway store worktree, then commits it with `git commit -q --no-verify -m 'commit scratch mapping (368f scenario 9)'`. The commit exits 1 because the tree is **clean** — `bridge_projects_set` left nothing to commit — so `subprocess.run(check=True)` raised.\n\nStory 368f documented the scenario's assumption explicitly: *\"`bridge_projects_set` writes the mapping to the WORKTREE but never commits it.\"* The \"nothing to commit\" failure means that assumption no longer holds — most likely `bridge_projects_set` now **auto-commits** the mapping itself (so the harness's explicit commit finds a clean tree), or it writes to a path the harness does not stage.\n\n## Regression window\nNEW regression, same window as sibling bug superior-pinelike-garpike:\n- 2026-08-15 run 31879125045 (jira DC job 94999114642): **73 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed**.\n- 2026-08-17 run 32000764439: **2 failed, 71 passed, 1 xfailed** — this is the second new failure.\n\nA change between 2026-08-15 and 2026-08-17 altered `bridge_projects_set`'s write/commit semantics (or the store-copy staging). Bisect `bridge_projects_set` and `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py` (cf. epic 0e68 / story 368f).\n\n## Impact\nThe multi-project capability-stamp + fail-closed live rehearsal is red. If `bridge_projects_set` changed to auto-commit, the behavior change is undocumented and the harness must be aligned; if the mapping write silently no-ops, it is a product regression. Either way the \"commit the mapping, then assert the capability stamp + fail-closed\" scenario cannot run.\n\n## The regression escaped because only a LIVE test covered it\nPer triage guidance: a live-external regression must be reproducible by a NON-external test so CI catches it without the live suite. Today only the live DC rehearsal exercises this.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Determine the actual post-change write semantics of `bridge_projects_set` (does it commit internally now, or leave a dirty tree?) — record the finding.\n- [ ] A **RED** non-external test (unit/integration, no live DC/creds) pins the intended `bridge_projects_set` write-and-commit contract (whether it commits, and what the worktree state is afterward) — asserted to FAIL against current `main` if this is a product regression; if the change is intended, the test encodes the NEW contract and the rehearsal harness is corrected to match.\n- [ ] Root cause fixed (product write path) OR harness/scenario corrected to the intended contract, with the reason recorded.\n- [ ] The new non-external test passes.\n- [ ] The live rehearsal `test_capability_stamp_and_fail_closed` passes in the next Live External Integration run.\n\n## Evidence\n- Failing run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32000764439 (job: jira DC harness smoke)\n- Test: `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py::test_capability_stamp_and_fail_closed`\n- Delivered by story 368f (gasolinic-microbian-puffin), epic 0e68 (outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","368f-f03e-a045-4377"],["relates_to","f643-db7d-3d9c-4bd3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b783-16ee-9520-4dda","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live Jira DC rehearsal: bridge_projects_set leaves nothing to commit — test_capability_stamp_and_fail_closed fails (git commit exit 1, 'nothing to commit')","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["181009ae-b84a-4ff8-9ad2-057ef34ce7b0","e731df12-a2e8-45f9-8b4a-d435ee98f99d","5bf42091-1145-4b1f-96dc-4c7dc3bbab09"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786999214436884001,"uuid":"dd898602-bbba-4c50-aea2-2f6406835446"}